    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment history shows sustained negative sentiment (e.g., multiple -0.25 or 0.00 values) and model overestimates.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to recent high prices (last 5-7 days) when sentiment shows bullish momentum (e.g., 0.50 or 0.00 followed by 0.00).",
    "Apply mean reversion correction if model consistently overpredicts prices after sharp spikes (e.g., >70.00) and true outcome drops below 65.00.",
    "Reduce forecast magnitude when sentiment shifts from bullish to neutral or bearish mid-period (e.g., 0.50 → 0.00 → -0.25).",
    "Add lag correction: if true outcome is higher than model forecast, adjust forecast upward by 0.5–1.0 units for next period if sentiment remains neutral or bullish.",
    "Avoid over-optimism in early periods (e.g., first 5 days of new history) — model should be conservative unless sentiment is strongly bullish."
  ]
